# Real-hardware config fragment: layered on top of sdkconfig.defaults it
# builds against the real adc_oneshot driver (main/lab_adc_oneshot.c) instead of
# adc_sim. Build the board variant in its OWN build directory, so the
# QEMU build in build/ stays as it is (from this project's directory):
#
#   idf.py -B build-hw -D SDKCONFIG=build-hw/sdkconfig \
#       -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw" build
#   idf.py -B build-hw -D SDKCONFIG=build-hw/sdkconfig -p <port> flash monitor
#
# (The defaults only apply when an sdkconfig is created, and idf.py
# remembers the list in the build directory -- so in build/ this layer
# would be silently ignored.) Not usable in QEMU, which has no such device.
# CONFIG_LAB_SIM_ADC is not set
